cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'Fetch PHP'
message: 'If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.'
authors:
  - family-names: Thayananthajothy
    given-names: Jerome
    email: tjthavarshan@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/Thavarshan/fetch-php
url: https://fetch-php.thavarshan.com
license: MIT
version: 3.8.0
date-released: '2026-07-22'
abstract: >-
  Fetch PHP is a modern PHP HTTP client library inspired by the JavaScript fetch API.
  Built on top of Guzzle, it provides a clean async/await interface using PHP Fibers,
  a PSR-7/PSR-18 compliant request/response model, middleware pipeline, lifecycle
  events and hooks, RFC 7234 HTTP caching, connection pooling, HTTP/2 support,
  streaming responses, Server-Sent Events parsing, and comprehensive testing utilities.
keywords:
  - php
  - http
  - http-client
  - fetch
  - fetch-api
  - async
  - promises
  - fibers
  - guzzle
  - psr-7
  - psr-18
  - psr-3
  - middleware
  - streaming
  - server-sent-events
  - caching
  - rest-api
